    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). \n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line now includes `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber` alongside the fields it already logged (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`).\n\nThe change is confined to a single method in `AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Added the two new placeholders/values to the `AUDIT.info(...)` call, reusing the existing `OwnerMembershipLevel.of(owner)` for the level.\n- Added a small private `membershipNumber(owner)` helper mirroring the mapper's formula (`customerCode + \"-M\" + last-two-year-digits`, null when either input is absent).\n\nStructural impact stayed minimal: one file touched, one existing (CC-1) method changed, with the new logic isolated in its own small cohesive helper rather than growing the existing method's complexity.",
